* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell and python must never get CRLF: a shebang followed by \r is "bad
# interpreter", which is a confusing way to learn about line endings.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.env   text eol=lf
bin/*   text eol=lf

*.img   binary
*.bin   binary

# brain/INDEX.md is GENERATED, and git must not try to merge it.
#
# Its content is a function of the whole note set, but a three-way merge is
# line-wise, so two branches that each add a note merge cleanly into a file
# that is wrong: both rows survive, and the `By scope` totals -- which each
# branch incremented from 123 to 124 independently, producing identical text
# -- do not. The result claims 124 where the merged tree holds 125.
#
# Nobody can debug that from the branch, because the branch is consistent.
# It appears only in the merge commit CI builds for a pull request, so it
# reads as "passes here, fails on CI" and it cost four CI rounds once.
#
# `-merge` makes any concurrent change a conflict instead. The resolution is
# not to edit it: run `make brain-index` and commit what it writes.
brain/INDEX.md  -merge
